    "raw_text": "Welcome to “Nick in Your Neighborhood,” a video series showcasing local businesses and exploring hidden gems in the community. The series highlights the unique stories, services, and community impact of these notable assets in Allegheny County and reinforces my commitment to supporting small businesses as a key legislative priority in the Senate. By featuring entrepreneurs and their contributions to the local economy, “Nick in Your Neighborhood” aims to encourage local patronage, promote economic growth, support workforce development, and underscore the importance of small businesses in building strong, vibrant communities.\nNominate a Business for “Nick in Your Neighborhood”\nArabica Robusta Coffee House\nGrab a cup and come along for the latest “Nick in Your Neighborhood” as I visit Arabica Robusta Coffee House, a woman-owned coffee shop bringing something brew-tiful to 8th Avenue in Homestead.\nOwner Hannah Kemp has created more than a place to grab your morning coffee. Arabica Robusta is a welcoming space to meet with friends, get some work done, or gather for meetings, networking events, birthdays, and celebrations. They make as much as possible in-house, including their own syrups, and created a custom Homestead Blend of Arabica and Robusta beans inspired by the neighborhood they call home.\nAs Arabica Robusta celebrates its first year, it’s already becoming part of the fabric of the community. With great coffee and a space built to bring people together, Hannah has found the perfect blend for keeping Homestead buzzing!\nLearn more about Arabica Robusta Coffee House at\nhttps://www.arabicarobustapgh.com\n.\nFollow them on social media.\nFollow\nFollow\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Arabica Robusta Coffee House\nSep 22, 2026\nNick in Your Neighborhood: FreeStyle Beauty Salon\nAug 31, 2026\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Joyful Commons\nMay 14, 2026\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Balena Bagels\nApr 17, 2026\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Outer Limits Adventure Park\nDec 2, 2025\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Brave Bean Coffee\nNov 6, 2025\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Firewhistle Brewing\nOct 7, 2025\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Sylvester & Tweeties Restaurant\nSep 11, 2025\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Willow Golf & Ice Cream\nAug 20, 2025\nNick in Your Neighborhood: Patti’s Pasticceria\nJun 12, 2025\nNominate a Business for “Nick in Your Neighborhood”\nDo you know a standout small business in the\n45th District\n? Help me shine a spotlight on the local entrepreneurs who make our community special by nominating them to be featured in “Nick in Your Neighborhood,” a video series dedicated to celebrating the hidden gems, hometown favorites, and hardworking businesses that drive our local economy.\nEach episode of “Nick in Your Neighborhood” showcases a new business and explores their positive impact on the community. This initiative is part of my commitment to supporting small businesses as a legislative priority in Harrisburg.\nBy featuring these local entrepreneurs, the series encourages community support, promotes economic growth, and reinforces the essential role small businesses play in building strong, vibrant neighborhoods.\nNominate a business today and help me share their story!\nNick in Your Neighborhood\nFirst Name\n*\nLast Name\n*\nAddress\n*\nAddress 2\nCity\n*\nState\n*\nAlabama\nAlaska\nArizona\nArkansas\nCalifornia\nColorado\nConnecticut\nDelaware\nDistrict of Columbia\nFlorida\nGeorgia\nHawaii\nIdaho\nIllinois\nIndiana\nIowa\nKansas\nKentucky\nLouisiana\nMaine\nMaryland\nMassachusetts\nMichigan\nMinnesota\nMississippi\nMissouri\nMontana\nNebraska\nNevada\nNew Hampshire\nNew Jersey\nNew Mexico\nNew York\nNorth Carolina\nNorth Dakota\nOhio\nOklahoma\nOregon\nPennsylvania\nRhode Island\nSouth Carolina\nSouth Dakota\nTennessee\nTexas\nUtah\nVermont\nVirginia\nWashington\nWest Virginia\nWisconsin\nWyoming\nZip Code\n*\nEmail\n*\nName of business being nominated\n*\nBusiness Address\n*\nBusiness Address 2\nCity\n*\nState\n*\nAlabama\nAlaska\nArizona\nArkansas\nCalifornia\nColorado\nConnecticut\nDelaware\nDistrict of Columbia\nFlorida\nGeorgia\nHawaii\nIdaho\nIllinois\nIndiana\nIowa\nKansas\nKentucky\nLouisiana\nMaine\nMaryland\nMassachusetts\nMichigan\nMinnesota\nMississippi\nMissouri\nMontana\nNebraska\nNevada\nNew Hampshire\nNew Jersey\nNew Mexico\nNew York\nNorth Carolina\nNorth Dakota\nOhio\nOklahoma\nOregon\nPennsylvania\nRhode Island\nSouth Carolina\nSouth Dakota\nTennessee\nTexas\nUtah\nVermont\nVirginia\nWashington\nWest Virginia\nWisconsin\nWyoming\nZip Code\n*\nWhy is this business is being nominated\n*\nIf you are human, leave this field blank.",
