    "raw_text": "Press Releases\nSenator Pisciottano Announces More Than $800,000 in Recreation & Conservation Investments\nMonroeville, PA – State Senator Nick Pisciottano today announced more than $800,000 in state funding for parks, recreation, and conservation initiatives benefiting Allegheny County through the Community Conservation Partnership Program administered by the Pennsylvania Department of Conservation...\nPisciottano’s Landmark AI Bill Establishes One of Nation’s First Advertising Disclosure Standards\nPA will become one of the 1st states in the nation to establish AI disclosure requirements to protect consumers from deceptive advertising under bipartisan legislation authored by Sen. Pisciottano.\nSenator Pisciottano Issues Statement in Support of Allegheny County Paid Parental Leave Proposal\nSen. Pisciottano released the following statement in support of Allegheny County’s revised paid parental leave proposal:\nSenator Pisciottano Announces $6.8 Million in Grants for Community Projects\nSen. Pisciottano announced $6,868,815 in LSA funding has been awarded to 28 projects to support public safety, infrastructure, parks & recreation, and municipal facilities projects.\nSenator Pisciottano Announces $5.3 Million for Victim Services in Allegheny County\nAllegheny County, PA – State Sen. Nick Pisciottano (D-Allegheny) announced that the Pennsylvania Commission on Crime and Delinquency (PCCD), chaired by Lieutenant Governor Austin Davis, has approved $5,333,957 in grant funding to support victims, strengthen public safety, and prevent violence. The...\nSenators Pisciottano and Kim Announce Legislation to Protect Pennsylvanians from Misuse of License Plate Reader Technology\nHarrisburg, PA – State Senators Nick Pisciottano (D-Allegheny) and Patty Kim (D-Dauphin) today announced plans to introduce legislation establishing statewide privacy and accountability standards for automated license plate reader systems, including Flock Safety cameras, as the technology...\nSenator Pisciottano Announces $6.75 Million in Grants for Economic Development, Education, Recreation, and Community Revitalization\nSen. Pisciottano announced $6.75 million in RACP grants to support community improvements, economic development, and infrastructure.\nSenator Pisciottano Announces Passage of State Budget\nSen. Pisciottano announced the passage of Pennsylvania’s 2026-27 state budget, a bipartisan spending plan that invests in Pennsylvania’s future while lowering costs for families and strengthening communities across the Commonwealth.\nSenate Passes Bipartisan Pisciottano-Culver Bill to License Medical Imaging Professionals, Strengthen Patient Safety\nThe Senate passed SB1334 sponsored by Sens. Pisciottano & Culver to establish licensing standards for medical imaging professionals & radiation therapists.\nSenate Unanimously Passes Bipartisan Pisciottano-Culver Bill to Update Nonprofit Reporting Requirements\nThe PA Senate passed legislation sponsored by Senators Pisciottano and Lynda Schlegel Culver to update financial reporting requirements for nonprofit organizations.\nPisciottano AI Transparency Bill Passes Senate with Overwhelming Bipartisan Support, Advances to House for Consideration\nSen. Pisciottano announced the Senate passed his legislation to increase transparency around the use of artificial intelligence in consumer advertising and sales.\nSenator Pisciottano Announces $1.3 Million in Community Safety Funding\nSen. Pisciottano announced $1,344,233 in funding approved for organizations serving Allegheny County through programs administered by PCCD.\nState and County Leaders Applaud Historic U.S. Steel Investment in the Mon Valley\nFollowing U.S. Steel and Nippon Steel’s announcement of a major investment in the Mon Valley Works, state and county leaders issued the following statement:\nSenator Pisciottano Announces $2.1 Million for School Safety Initiatives in Allegheny County\nSen. Pisciottano announced more than $2.1 million has been approved for school safety initiatives in Allegheny County.\nSenators Pisciottano and Saval Propose Protections for Homeowners Entering Shared Equity Agreements\nSens. Pisciottano and Saval have circulated a co-sponsorship memo for legislation regulating shared equity agreements, establishing consumer protections and oversight for a growing financial product tied to homeownership.\nSenator Pisciottano Announces Extension of Property Tax/Rent Rebate Deadline\nSen. Pisciottano is encouraging eligible Pennsylvanians to take advantage of the extended deadline for the Property Tax/Rent Rebate Program.\nSenator Pisciottano to Introduce Legislation to Help Small Businesses Provide Health Coverage\nSen. Pisciottano circulated a memo for legislation to establish a tax credit for small businesses to contribute to their employees’ health insurance premiums.\nPisciottano AI Transparency Bill Advances Unanimously\nSen. Pisciottano announced his legislation has been unanimously reported out of the Senate Communications and Technology Committee with bipartisan support.\nSenator Pisciottano Announces Nearly $1.75 Million for Violence Prevention and Youth Program Grants\nMonroeville, PA – State Senator Nick Pisciottano (D-Allegheny) today announced that $1,747,897 in state funding has been awarded to organizations and schools across his district through the Pennsylvania Commission on Crime and Delinquency’s (PCCD) Violence Intervention & Prevention (VIP) and...\nLeaders Announce Almost $15 Million Investment to Replace Versailles Avenue Viaduct in McKeesport\nMcKeesport, PA – Federal, state, and local leaders gathered today at the closed Versailles Avenue Viaduct in McKeesport to announce a $14.75 million investment to replace it and restore a critical connection for thousands of residents and commuters. The nearly 300-foot-long bridge has been closed...\n« Older Entries\nNewsroom\n→ Press Releases\n→ Newsletters\n→ Video\n→ Live Web Stream\n→ Podcasts\n→ Petitions and Remonstrances",
