    "title": "Nick in Your Neighborhood: Joyful Commons",
    "url": "https://pasenatornick.com/joyful-commons/",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Joyful Commons\nFor this stop on “Nick in Your Neighborhood,” I visit Joyful Commons in Homestead, a one-of-a-kind coworking and play space designed with working parents in mind. Founded by entrepreneur and Pittsburgh mom Jade Granda, Joyful Commons was created from the realization that parents shouldn’t have to choose between raising a family and pursuing their goals.\nBlending historic charm with a flexible, family-first design, Joyful Commons offers a space where parents can answer emails, hold meetings, or enjoy a cup of coffee while their children play safely nearby. Through every detail, Jade has woven together comfort, creativity, and peace of mind for busy families balancing parenthood and work.\nIn a world where spaces like this are still uncommon, Jade is creating a place where productivity and playtime have something in common.\nLearn more about Joyful Commons at\nwww.joyfulcommons.com\n.\nFollow them on social media.\nFollow\nFollow",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "A Pennsylvania legislator visited Joyful Commons, a coworking space in Homestead that provides childcare-adjacent facilities for working parents, as part of a district outreach tour called 'Nick in Your Neighborhood.' The visit highlighted the small business, founded by Jade Granda, which combines workspace for adults with a supervised play area for children. No legislation, funding, or official action was announced.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "economy",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
