    "raw_text": "About\nLearn more about Senator Nick Pisciottano.\nLearn More\nContact Me\nConcerned about an issue? Need help with a state agency? If I can help in any way, please reach out!\nContact Me\nLatest News\nStay up-to-date with the latest releases, videos, and more.\nLearn More\nServices & Resources\nMy office takes great pride in assisting constituents. Need help with something? Let my office help.\nCheck out our services\nHow Can We Help?\nMy office takes great pride in assisting constituents. Need help with something? We will give our best effort to help.\nContact Me\nProperty Tax/Rent Rebate Services\nVehicle Services\nPA Grant & Resource Directory\nARE YOU READY\nTO VOTE IN 2026?\nLatest News\nLawmakers Launch New Kids & Families Caucus\nPlum, PA – October 14, 2026 −\nState\nSenator Nick Pisciottano\n(D-45, Allegheny) and State Representatives\nAerion Abney\n(D-19, Allegheny) and\nJennifer O’Mara\n(D-165, Delaware) were joined by\nLieutenant Governor Austin Davis\n,\nAllegheny County Executive Sara Innamorato\n, and local officials Wednesday at the Sampson Family YMCA in Plum to announce the formation of the Pennsylvania General Assembly’s new\nKids & Families Caucus\n.\nread more\nSenator Pisciottano Announces More Than $800,000 in Recreation & Conservation Investments\nMonroeville, PA – State Senator Nick Pisciottano today announced more than $800,000 in state funding for parks, recreation, and conservation...\nread more\nPisciottano’s Landmark AI Bill Establishes One of Nation’s First Advertising Disclosure Standards\nPA will become one of the 1st states in the nation to establish AI disclosure requirements to protect consumers from deceptive advertising under bipartisan legislation authored by Sen. Pisciottano.\nread more\nView All\nStay In the Know with E-updates!\nStay “In the Know with Nick Pisciottano” by using the form below to sign up for his electronic newsletter and get the latest news and updates from the district and around the state!",
